  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-22T09:22:32.055Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A Canvas that has been attached with VRC_UiShape can be controlable with a blue raycast beam.\nIn usual case, This beam can be kept appearing even the distance between the hand and the canvas is almost zero, when Canvas's Scale Z has small value like 0.001.\nBut, when the Canvas component and UdonBehaviour component has attached at a same GameObject, this blue beam will disappears at a certain distance.\nThis mysterious distance makes the operation of the UI difficult, and also prevents that people realizing spontaneously how to use those UIs.\nReproduction world here: \nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_bcf0c335-0daf-4cd9-ac0d-0ffc09f8f53e\nNote:\nThis problem can be avoided by attach UdonBehaviour to another GameObject out of Canvas Hierarchy, but this is unuseful when making prefabs for distribute Canvas-based Udon assets.",
